# Coding Style

## Vue

- `<script setup lang="ts">` everywhere; no Options API
- Typed props and emits
- Presentational components — call Engine for mutations, read state via `useGameState()`

## TypeScript

- TypeScript only; no `.js` source files
- `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions/aliases
- Avoid classes unless wrapping third-party libs
- Prefer named exports (Vue SFCs may use default)

## Imports

Path aliases: `@engine/*`, `@state/*`, `@ui/*`, `@data/*`, `@/types`, `@/services/*`

## Naming

- Engine exports: `engineAdvanceTurn`, `engineSpawnCharacter` (from `src/engine/index.ts`)
- Engine internals: `advanceTurn`, `spawnFromTemplate` (domain verbs)
- Pinia stores: `useUiStore`, `use<Name>Store`
- Types: PascalCase nouns (`GameState`, `ItemDefinition`)

## Files

- One primary export per Engine module
- `<style scoped>` with components
- JSON filenames: kebab-case
